  "id": "BIT-phpmyadmin-2026-119562",
  "summary": "phpMyAdmin through 5.2.3 SQL Injection via Central Columns col_extra and col_attribute",
  "details": "phpMyAdmin through 5.2.3 contains an sql injection vulnerability that allows authenticated users to inject SQL by supplying unescaped col_extra and col_attribute values to /database/central-columns. Attackers can inject SQL into pma__central_columns INSERT and UPDATE queries run with controluser privileges, reading or modifying other users' configuration-storage data.",
